  "title": "AJILE12: long-term naturalistic ECoG with wrist-movement events and behaviour labels (DANDI 000055)",
  "description": "AJILE12 comprises long-term naturalistic electrocorticography (ECoG) recorded passively from 12 participants during clinical epilepsy monitoring at Harborview Medical Center, totaling 55 recording days (about 1295 h). The recordings are paired with video-derived pose estimates, visually validated wrist-movement initiation events, and coarse behavioural state labels. This iEEG-BIDS version converts the original NWB release from DANDI 000055 without changing signal values, and there is no experimental task.",
  "methods_description": "ECoG (grids, strips and some depth electrodes) was recorded at 1 kHz with simultaneous 30 fps video during 24-hour clinical monitoring on days 3-7 after implantation. The authors applied median DC removal, 1-200 Hz band-pass, 60 Hz notch, downsampling to 500 Hz and common median re-referencing per electrode group. Electrodes were localised with FieldTrip by co-registering pre-operative MRI and post-operative CT, then warped to MNI space. Upper-body pose was estimated from the video, and wrist-movement events and coarse behaviour labels were annotated.",
